6/BooksAll.2016.part26.utf8:69761192:1087","ia:bridgeofquiescen0000wall","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-08-26","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-005.mrc:124970860:2984","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_021.bib.mrc:40879409:3499"],"title":"The bridge of quiescence","dewey_decimal_class":["294.3/4435"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (p. 311-323) and index\nIncludes the text of Tsoṅ-kha-pa Blo-bzaṅ-grags-pa's text of Byang chub lam gyi rim pa chung ba."},"identifiers":{"librarything":["536725"],"goodreads":["645979","2748987"]},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lccn":["97041697"],"subjects":["Tsoṅ-kha-pa Blo-bzaṅ-grags-pa, 1357-1419","Lam-rim","Meditation -- Buddhism"],"publish_date":"1998","publish_country":"ilu","by_statement":"B. Alan Wallace ; foreword by H.H. the Dalai Lama.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL18250163W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"ocaid":"bridgeofquiescen0000wall","local_id":["urn:bwbsku:P7-AKW-118"],"oclc_numbers":["37837608"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"This challenging new work examines practical techniques for training the attention. It will be of interest to seasoned contemplatives, to general readers concerned with meditation, to philosophers of mind, and to cognitive scientists.\n\nThe book includes a translation, with commentary, of Tsongkhapa's classic fifteenth-century discussion of methods for developing exceptionally high degrees of attentional stability and clarity. Such enhancement and refining of the attention is an indispensable prerequisite to rigorous, introspective enquiry into the nature of the mind. Insights gleaned from such enquiry are instrumental in identifying and eliminating the inner sources of anxiety, frustration, and discontent.\n\nTo place this training in its traditional context, Professor Wallace explains Tsongkhapa's methodology and presents an overview of Tsongkhapa's vision of reality.\n\nThe Bridge of Quiescence affords a bridge from Eastern meditative practice to Western philosophy, science, and religion. Wallace's discussion draws upon his knowledge of experimental psychology (such as sensory deprivation studies) and relates Tibetan meditation to discussions of consciousness by such Western thinkers as William James, William Christian, and John Searle."},"latest_revision":18,"revision":18,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-11-04T17:18:25.868780"}}},"ISBN:9780812693614":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780812693614","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL694392M/The_bridge_of_quiescence","preview":"borrow","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/bridgeofquiescen0000wall","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4706397-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Open Court"],"number_of_pages":336,"subtitle":"experiencing Tibetan Buddhist meditation","isbn_10":["0812693604","0812693612"],"covers":[4706397,3791050,604741],"lc_classifications":["BQ7950.T754 B9338 1998","BQ7950.T754B9338"],"key":"/books/OL694392M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL26553A","name":"B. Alan Wallace"}],"publish_places":["Chicago"],"contributions":["Tsoṅ-kha-pa Blo-bzaṅ-grags-pa, 1357-1419."],"pagination":"xvi, 336 p. ;","source_records":["marc:marc_records_scriblio_net/part26.dat:147125429:1081","marc:marc_ithaca_college/ic_marc.mrc:161412180:1119","amazon:0812693612","bwb:9780812693614","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part26.utf8:69761192:1087","ia:bridgeofquiescen0000wall","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-08-26","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-005.mrc:124970860:2984","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_021.bib.mrc:40879409:3499"],"title":"The bridge of quiescence","dewey_decimal_class":["294.3/4435"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (p. 311-323) and index\nIncludes the text of Tsoṅ-kha-pa Blo-bzaṅ-grags-pa's text of Byang chub lam gyi rim pa chung ba."